--TEST--
A declaration whose initializer is `&$x` is `E0701`, like the assignment it spells, and never a parse error — `rule:types/implicit-capture`, `rule:classes/two-copy-depths`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// A declaration's initializer is not an assignment expression, so the parser
// reports the `&` itself, and the value after it is still type-checked: each
// line below is exactly one error.
int $a = 1;
int $b = &$a;
var $c = &$a;
for (int $i = &$a; $i < 3; $i++) {
    echo $i, "\n";
}
--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0701]: a binding cannot be assigned by reference
  --> %s:6:5
  |
6 | int $b = &$a;
  |     ^^^^^^^^ this would share `$a`'s own slot
%A
error[E0701]: a binding cannot be assigned by reference
  --> %s:7:5
  |
7 | var $c = &$a;
  |     ^^^^^^^^ this would share `$a`'s own slot
%A
error[E0701]: a binding cannot be assigned by reference
  --> %s:8:10
  |
8 | for (int $i = &$a; $i < 3; $i++) {
  |          ^^^^^^^^ this would share `$a`'s own slot
%A
error: aborting due to 3 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
